{"name":"Burrito","hex":"#eed7c1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burrito","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Mexican dish consisting of a flour tortilla wrapped around a filling of meat and/or beans, cheese etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wrap someone or something up like a burrito."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burrito"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burrito","blocks":[{"text":"A burrito or burro is historically a regional name in Mexico for what in other parts of the country is known as a taco. The term burrito was regional, specifically from Guanajuato, Guerrero, Michoacán, San Luis Potosí, Sonora and Sinaloa, for what is known as a taco in Mexico City and surrounding areas, and codzito in Yucatán and Quintana Roo. Due to the cultural influence of Mexico City, the term taco became the default, and the meaning of terms like burrito and codzito were forgotten, leading many people to create new meanings and folk histories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Burrito.JPG/330px-Burrito.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burrito"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shredded_pork_burrito.jpg/500px-Shredded_pork_burrito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shredded_pork_burrito.jpg/500px-Shredded_pork_burrito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mission-style burrito containing shredded pork, beans, and rice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShredded_pork_burrito.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Carne-asada-burrito.jpg/500px-Carne-asada-burrito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped